The full suite list ran on a scratch copy of HEAD 260937a (git archive into <scratch>/p2-scratch/verify-S3-1; log in verify-S3-logs/suite-1.log), and everything passed:
- gofmt -l . reports nothing outside review/, and also nothing in the worktree, which is clean at 260937a.
- go vet and go build pass for the root module and for ui.
- GOLEDGER_CHAOS_SLACK=4 go test -race -count=1 ./... passed twice: consensus 55.2 s and 56.2 s, ledger 11.0 s and 10.4 s, node 52.8 s and 52.1 s.
- The same with -C ui passed twice, in 30.3 s and 29.8 s.
- The -count=3 Chaos|Restart|SignLog|Resume|CatchUp run passed in 93.2 s.

All 21 listed tests exist, plus TestApplyBlockRefusesAPaymentBelowTheCost for rule 17's cost floor.

I ran about 78 mutants of my own (harness verify-S3-tools/mutate.py; results in verify-S3-logs/mutants1.out to mutants6.out). Each is a single edit in a fresh copy of HEAD. Every listed test fails under the mutant for the change it covers:
- names, a payment under any account's key, an unknown payee, a frozen payer or payee, the cost floor;
- "-" stored literally, Delegate ignored, the four delegation checks;
- digest field, tag and order; NamesAscending with > instead of >=;
- a frozen name seated in either mode, frozen stake backing a delegate, a seat with no account, a reassignment to a new name;
- MinMessageBytes 4900 and a default of 6300;
- VoteSet and Commit under any key in the set;
- the checkpoint and genesis order checks, the one-third anchor floor, a receipt for a repeat or by key, 202 on a refused update, intake under any key for payments and updates;
- the governance view by key, resolve without bank or frozen, the locked proposal under the node's own key;
- the wallet's name, recipient, delegate, pin-name and state-order checks;
- in cmd/server: the validator account, the sort, the node name, genesis names and delegates, and the default bound.

The mutants that survived are the problems listed. Two survivors are harmless: removing the anchor's key-equality check is safe because step 4 verifies under the same key, and the wallet's pinnedKey != "" test is redundant.

Message sizes match spec 4.1: the largest payment is 4961 bytes, or 6361 escaped.

An end-to-end run of the demo with the built wallet UI:
- A payment to bakery got "receipt from validator founder verified".
- "Bakery" was refused.
- A delegate with no account showed the node's 409 reason.
- "-" cleared the delegate, and the new description landed in state.

I checked the §10.2 S3 scope item by item against §3–§8, and reviewed deviations 1 to 11. Each defers to the slice the spec assigns (pin to S4, rules 21 and 24 and L to S5, GenesisHash and SignedProposal to S4, bank and ValidateGenesis to S8, wallet display to S9) or is the smallest reading; deviation 6, the locked proposal checked under its proposer's key, is correct. Nothing from a later slice is half-built. The only leftover wire tag is on Block, which S4 redefines. Names follow the spelled-out rule; the short name `me` predates S3. Scratch tests that show each problem are under p2-scratch/verify-S3-2 and verify-S3-parent.

secondCheck.evidence:
S3 is confirmed. HEAD is 3913843 and the worktree is clean. All my experiments ran in scratch copies under <scratch>/p2-scratch/ (verify-S3-r2-*). Logs are in its verify-S3-r2-logs/ folder and the mutant harness is verify-S3-r2-tools/mutate.py.

**Problem 1 (anchorVouches) is fixed.**
- anchorVouches now marks a name as checked before verifying its vote, so each anchor name costs at most one signature check (spec 4.14 step 3).
- Reverting just that change makes TestAnchorChecksOneVotePerName fail with 24 checks against its bound of 6 (batch1.out).
- My own test (verify-S3-r2-adv/node/zz_verifier_anchor_test.go) used 7 anchor names, each padded with 30 junk copies signed under other keys plus 50 stranger votes:
  - junk votes first: 7 checks;
  - genuine votes first: 14 checks, exactly the bound of anchor names plus carried set (7 + 7);
  - the unpadded genuine checkpoint still verifies.
- No valid checkpoint can be refused: Commit.Verify already refuses a name that appears twice, before verifying it.
- The fixer left out the optional shape check before verifying. That is correct: Commit.Verify refuses a wrong-shaped vote anyway, so the check would change neither the verdict nor the bound.

**Problem 2 (key looked up by name) is fixed.** Each mutant below makes its named test fail (batch1.out):
- update verified under any account's key: TestUpdateDelegatesToAName (ProposeBlock carried the update);
- reassignment vote verified under any key in the set: TestReassignmentRequiresTwoThirds;
- proposal verified under any key in the set: TestProposalIsTakenOnlyFromTheRoundProposer;
- proposal accepted under any proposer name: TestProposalIsTakenOnlyFromTheRoundProposer;
- vote counted under any key in the set: TestOnlyCountableVotesAreKeptAndRelayed;
- the loop's key re-check removed, for payments or for updates: TestLoopRechecksTheSignersKey;
- a config with neither validators nor a threshold accepted: TestLoadRefusesAConfigWithoutValidatorsOrThreshold;
- the intake comment-length check removed: TestIntakeRefusesAnOverlongComment;
- the wallet route left at /register: TestAccountFormDelegates.

The new tests pass 10 times in a row under -race.

**Full suite, my own run on 3913843** (suite-1.log):
- gofmt -l (review/ excluded) prints nothing; vet and build pass for both modules.
- `GOLEDGER_CHAOS_SLACK=4 go test -race -count=1 ./...` passes twice (consensus 56.5 s and 57.7 s, node 52.3 s and 51.8 s, ledger 10.4 s).
- The same for ui passes twice (32.1 s, 30.1 s).
- The chaos run (`-race -count=3 -run 'Chaos|Restart|SignLog|Resume|CatchUp' ./node/`) passes in 92.6 s.
- No data race was reported in any run.

**Re-check of the whole slice.**
- Every S3 scope item in spec 10.2 is present, and all 21 tests the slice lists exist.
- I re-applied the first round's 76 mutants to HEAD (batch2.out). Every mutant aimed at a listed test is still killed. The survivors fall into three groups:
  - ledger changes run against the node or ui tests, which the ledger tests do kill;
  - equivalent mutants (anchor without verify, receipt pinned-key check, wallet pinned set, lastCommit set);
  - gaps that already existed in the parent: the update BlockID rule has no ledger test, and nothing tests the late double-sign check. I confirmed both on f2e257e (batch7-parent.out); S6 rewrites the late double-sign code.
- What is signed and hashed matches the spec: the payment fields (spec 4.1), the update fields (4.2), the payment and update ids, and the accounts digest (3.5, checked by the hand-built golden test).
- Message sizes match spec 4.1: the largest payment is 4961 bytes, or 6361 with every comment byte escaped.
- Config matches spec 6.1.
- The builder's deviations are each justified by a later slice's scope.
- No later slice is half-built, and I found no code with no production caller beyond the existing test helpers SubmitPayment and SubmitUpdate.
- Demo end to end works (demo-e2e.sh):
  - paying bakery by name gives a receipt the wallet verifies as founder's;
  - "Bakery" is refused as not a name;
  - a description update lands, and "-" clears it;
  - /hdls/resolve shows the bank and frozen fields;
  - /hdls/update answers 409 with the reason.

The two problems listed are both minor.
